          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The term
            %em holographic entanglement entropy
            refers to expressions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theories"} quantum field theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+duality"} AdS-CFT duality
            (“holography”), in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            of a higher-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %p
            The essential idea is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            of a region
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            in the domain of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            should be proportional to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length"}> length
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/area"} area
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypersurface"} hypersurface
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            which shares the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi U
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial U = \partial \Sigma
            and which has minimal volume with this property. A more precise version of this idea is given by the
            = succeed "," do
              %em Ryu-Takayanagi formula
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagiFormula"} below
          %p
            This kind of relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropy"} entropy
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+systems"} quantum systems
            and
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/area"} area
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volumes"} volumes
            of critical surfaces in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curved+spacetime"} curved spacetime
            is akin to the
            = succeed "-formula" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
            %em subsume
            the
            = succeed "-formula" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+entropy"} black hole entropy
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetimes"} anti de Sitter spacetimes
          %p
            While in the original context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            the Ryu-Takayanagi formula remains ill-defined, or at least intractable in detail (not the least because it is, ultimately, a statement about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "M-theory#TheOpenProblem"} remains elusive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+networks"} tensor networks
            that express (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/code+subspaces"}> code subspaces
            ) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correcting+codes"} quantum error correcting codes
            (such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+dimer+codes"} Majorana dimer codes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            models the behaviour of holographic entanglement entropy, and of several other expected aspects of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holography"} holography
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                from
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
            %li
              %p
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/condensed+matter+physics"} condensed matter physics
                (see also at
                = succeed ")." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCMT"} AdS/CMT
          %p
            The power of these
            = succeed "-methods" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holography"} holographic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            has re-inforced the earlier idea in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            that notions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            may be holographically defined and in fact
            %em emerge
            from non-gravitational
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+physics"} quantum physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+entanglement"} quantum entanglement
            – an idea that has become known under the slogan “
            %a{:href => "#SimonsFoundationItFromQBit"}> It from Qbit
            ” (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Georgescu19"} Georgescu 19
            %em extra
            (higher)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensions
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            typically relies on some notion domain space(-time) already (maybe unless one considers bulk duals of
            = succeed "\u2026)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%28-1%29-branes"} D(-1)-branes
          %h3#RyuTakayanagiFormula Ryu-Takayanagi formula
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theories"} quantum field theories
            that are exhibited as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theories"} boundary field theories
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of an approximately
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            via some approximation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+duality"} AdS-CFT duality
            (for instance for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            via
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-QCD+duality"} AdS-QCD duality
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            of a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+set"} bounded domain
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\subset A
            turns out to be proportional to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/area"}> area
            ) of the minimal-area
            = succeed "-2" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypersurface"} hypersurface
            inside the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            spacetime that has the same
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial B
            (see
            %a{:href => "#NishiokaRyuTakayanagi09"} Nishioka-Ryu-Takayanagi 09 (3.3)
            for review of the formula and
            %a{:href => "#LewkowyczMaldacena13"} Lewkowycz-Maldacena 13
            for a conceptual explanation).
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/RyuTakayanagiFormula.jpg", :width => "520"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#NishiokaRyuTakayanagi09"} Nishioka-Ryu-Takayanagi 09
          %p
            This relation is known as the
            %em Ryu-Takayanagi formula
            (
            %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagi06a"}> Ryu-Takayanagi 06a
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagi06b"} Ryu-Takayanagi 06b
            = succeed "," do
              %em holographic entanglement entropy
          %p
            This is a generalization of the proportionality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+entropy"} black hole entropy
            to the area of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/event+horizon"} event horizon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+duality"} AdS-CFT duality
            applies to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/near+horizon+geometry"} near horizon geometry
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
            and reduces 4d black holes under suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            (see also at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/RyuTakayanagiBlackHoleEntropy.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#NishiokaRyuTakayanagi09"} Nishioka-Ryu-Takayanagi 09
          %p
            In fact quantum corrections to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+entropy"} black hole entropy
            in the presence of matter fields is equal to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagi06a"} Ryu-Takayanagi 06a, p. 13
          %p
            Various properties of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            find immediate geometric interpretations this way, for instance subadditivity
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/RyuTakayanagiSubadditivity.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#NishiokaRyuTakayanagi09"} Nishioka-Ryu-Takayanagi 09
          %h3#TensorNetworkModels Tensor network models
          %p
            Further discussion of implications of the Ryu-Takayanagi formula in
            %a{:href => "#vanRaamsdonk10"} van Raamsdonk 10
            suggested that the logic may also be turned around: Instead of computing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            of a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            from known
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            may be reconstructed from knowledge of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement+entropy"} entanglement entropy
            of a boundary field theory.
          %p
            Talking this perspective to the extreme suggests a description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            entirely in terms of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+information+theory"} quantum information theory
            = succeed "-relations" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement"} entanglement
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT"} QFT
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+networks"}> tensor networks
            ”,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Swingle09"} Swingle 09
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Swingle12"} Swingle 12
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correction+codes"} quantum error correction codes
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#ADH14"} ADH 14
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#PYHP15"} PYHP 15
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HNQTWY16"} HNQTWY 16
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Harlow18"} Harlow 18
            %a{:href => "#JahnEisert21"} Jahn-Eisert 21
            for review).
          %p
            Here a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré dual
            to a finite-stage
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+tesselation"} hyperbolic tesselation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+plane"} hyperbolic plane
            is interpreted as a discretized model for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            with holographic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            on its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            being given by the
            = succeed "-evaluation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+diagram"} string diagram
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of spaces corresonding to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
            crossing the boundary of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tesselation"} tesselation
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 20px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HaPPYCodeTesselation.jpg", :width => "480px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#Harlow18"} Harlow 18
          %p
            One shows (
            %a{:href => "#ADH14"}> ADH 14
            ) that this is a decent (“toy”) model of expected properties of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holography"} holography
            if this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/code+subspace"} code subspace
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correcting+code"} quantum error correcting code
          %p
            For example, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            corresponding to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pentagon"} pentagonal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 5
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{5,4\}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tesselation"} tesselation
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+tensor"} perfect tensor
            of rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 5
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 5+1
            assigned to each tile yields a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correcting+code"} quantum error correcting code
            now known as the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
          %p
            The idea is that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/code+subspace"} code subspace
            of this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
            is that subspace of the boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            which holographically corresponds to all bulk states
            %em without
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            in the bulk.
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/BlackHoleInHaPPYCodeTensorNetworkII.jpg", :width => "360px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#JahnEisert21"} Jahn  Eisert 21
          %p
            More generally, deleting any of the tiles in the interior of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tesselation"} tesselation
            is interpreted as the appearance of a bulk
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
            is carried by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+states"} quantum states
            carried by the loose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
            that cross over the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/event+horizon"}> event horizon
            ” to the now deleted tiles.
          %p
            The extreme case that
            %em all
            tiles are deleted from the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            that has swallowed up the entire
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
            spacetime such that its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizon"} horizon
            now coincides with the previous
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
          %p
            %br/
          %p
            In this discrete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
            model for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            the Ryu-Takayanagi formula for holographic entanglement entropy (
            %a{:href => "#RyuTakayanagiFormula"}> above
            ) has an exact proof
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#PYHP15"} PYHP 15, Theorem 2
          %h3#ChordDiagramRepresentation Chord diagram representation
          %p
            In fact, holographic entanglement entropy in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
            turns out to be entirely encoded by the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimer"} dimer
              network
            in the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+dimer+code"} Majorana dimer code
            (
            %a{:href => "#JGPE19"}> JGPE 19
            ):
          %div{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HaPPYCodesAsDimerCode.jpg", :width => "680px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#JGPE19"} JGPE 19
          %p
            in that the entanglement entropy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_A
            of any
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+dimer+code"} Majorana dimer code
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+network"} tensor network
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} state
            turns out to count the number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimers"} dimers
            that cross between the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"}> connected
            ) subregion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and its
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
          %div{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/ChordDiagramEntanglementEntropy.jpg", :width => "460px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#JGPE19"} JGPE 19
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HanUniversalHolographicCode.jpg", :width => "400px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                From
                %a{:href => "#Yan20"} Yan 20
          %p
            In the case that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimers"} dimers
            correspond to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+tesselation"} hyperbolic tesselation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 5
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{5,4\}
            from the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %mi ln
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo |
                      %mi Chords
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo |
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_A
                  \\;=\;
                  \\tfrac{1}{2}
                  \\ln
                  \\big(
                  2^{ \left\vert Chords(A, \bar A) \right\vert }
                  \\big)
          %p
            recovers the Ryu-Takayanagi formula (
            %a{:href => "#JGPE19"}> JGPE 19 (78)
            ), as here the number of chords crossing any hyperbolic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
            grows linearly with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/length"} length
            of this geodesic.
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuum+limit"} continuum limit
            this says that holographic entanglement entropy is exhibited by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flow"} flow
            out of the given subregion through its corresponding minimal bulk surface, an idea that was previously proposed in “bit-thread models” for holographic entanglement entropy (
            %a{:href => "#FreedmanHeadrick16"}> Freedman &amp; Headrick 16
            ):
          %div{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/HyperbolicGeodesicFlowAndEntanglementEntropy.jpg", :width => "700px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#FreedmanHeadrick16"} Freedman  Headrick 16
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px 20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/ChordDiagram.jpg", :width => "300px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber19c"} Sati  Schreiber 19c
          %p
            Following
            %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber19c"} Sati-Schreiber 19c
            we recognize the above
            = succeed "/bit-thread" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+dimer"} Majorana dimer
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#JGPE19"} JGPE 19
            %a{:href => "#Yan19"} Yan 19
            as
            = succeed "-encodings" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagram"} chord diagram
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.10425v3.pdf#page=38"} p. 38
          %p
            Notice how each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord"} chord
            here reflects at the same time
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                one
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entanglement"} entangled pair
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/qbits"} qbits
                in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geodesic"} geodesic
                through the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hyperbolic+plane"} hyperbolic plane
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bulk"} bulk
                spacetime.
          %p
            This is a (rigorous) state of affairs reminiscent of the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ER+%3D+EPR"}> ER = EPR
            ” slogan.
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+Renyi+entropy"} holographic Renyi entropy
            %li
              %p gravitational entropy
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+second+law+of+thermodynamics"} generalized second law of thermodynamics
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ER+%3D+EPR"} ER = EPR
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+AdS-CFT"} p-adic AdS-CFT
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+error+correcting+code"} quantum error correcting code
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HaPPY+code"} HaPPY code
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+dimer+code"} Majorana dimer code
          %h2#References References
          %h3#general General
          %p The original articles are
          %ul
            %li#RyuTakayanagi06a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shinsei+Ryu"}> Shinsei Ryu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadashi+Takayanagi"} Tadashi Takayanagi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Holographic Derivation of Entanglement Entropy from AdS/CFT
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0603001"} arXiv:hep-th/0603001
            %li#RyuTakayanagi06a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shinsei+Ryu"}> Shinsei Ryu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadashi+Takayanagi"} Tadashi Takayanagi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Aspects of Holographic Entanglement Entropy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605073"} arXiv:hep-th/0605073
          %p A proposal for a conceptual explanation:
          %ul
            %li#LewkowyczMaldacena13
              %p
                Aitor Lewkowycz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"} Juan Maldacena
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized gravitational entropy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.4926"} arXiv:1304.4926
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nele+Callebaut"}> Nele Callebaut
                ,
                %em Entanglement in conformal field theory and holography
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.16827"}> arXiv:2303.16827
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
